345,peadswithdranum,2026-06-13T17:29:28.000Z,"RUBELLA (GERMAN MEASLES) Rubella is a mild, contagious viral illness caused by the Rubella virus (Rubivirus, Togaviridae family). It typically presents with a 3-day maculopapular rash, low-grade fever, and postauricular lymphadenopathy. Although usually self-limiting in children, infection during pregnancy can lead to Congenital Rubella Syndrome (CRS), causing severe fetal cardiac, ocular, and auditory defects. Vaccination with MMR/MMRV remains the most effective preventive strategy. 1/2 RUBELLA (GERMAN MEASLES) Rubella is a mild, contagious viral illness caused by the Rubella virus (Rubivirus, Togaviridae family). It typically presents with a 3-day maculopapular rash, low-grade fever, and postauricular lymphadenopathy. Although usually self-limiting in children, infection during pregnancy can lead to Congenital Rubella Syndrome (CRS), causing severe fetal cardiac, ocular, and auditory defects. Vaccination with MMR/MMRV remains the most effective preventive strategy. Soft Universe · AURORA",https://www.threads.com/@peadswithdranum/post/DZiNPvxjMwb,"",0,0,0,0,NaN
