383,lauras.write.edits,2025-02-22T03:02:30.000Z,"Since anti-vaxxers prefer anecdotal evidence rather than scientific, I am going to give anecdotal evidence to explain why I am pro-vaccines. Since anti-vaxxers prefer anecdotal evidence rather than scientific, I am going to give anecdotal evidence to explain why I am pro-vaccines. Gather round friends, and let me tell you about my grandma. Gather round friends, and let me tell you about my grandma. My grandma was born in 1934. As she grew up, she caught whooping cough, chicken pox, and rubella TWICE each. Yes, you read that right. Twice. One of my theories that her immune system got wiped out by measles at some point. (1) 1/4 My grandma was born in 1934. As she grew up, she caught whooping cough, chicken pox, and rubella TWICE each. Yes, you read that right. Twice. One of my theories that her immune system got wiped out by measles at some point. (1)",https://www.threads.com/@lauras.write.edits/post/DGW_pavs3Ja,"",0,0,1000,0,NaN
