432,ameracadpeds,2025-09-17T14:56:14.000Z,"ameracadpedsVerified The MMR and MMRV vaccines help children build immunity against serious diseases. While the MMR vaccine protects against measles, mumps and rubella, MMRV is a combination vaccine that provides additional immunity for varicella (or chickenpox). The MMR and MMRV vaccines help children build immunity against serious diseases. While the MMR vaccine protects against measles, mumps and rubella, MMRV is a combination vaccine that provides additional immunity for varicella (or chickenpox). Both vaccines are critical for keeping these vaccine-preventable diseases at bay. The AAP recommends parents discuss each option with their pediatrician to make the most informed decision for their children.  bit.ly/3UpYt… Both vaccines are critical for keeping these vaccine-preventable diseases at bay. The AAP recommends parents discuss each option with their pediatrician to make the most informed decision for their children. bit.ly/3UpYt…",https://www.threads.com/@ameracadpeds/post/DOtR3YsCuRs,"",0,0,0,0,NaN
