1402,morganl.whit,2026-07-13T19:18:22.000Z,"Yesterday at a kids’ play place, my beautiful black 4yo was playing with a 5yo girl of another ethnicity. An adorable little black boy ran by, and the girl looks at my daughter and says, “Ew. He looks creepy.” Yesterday at a kids’ play place, my beautiful black 4yo was playing with a 5yo girl of another ethnicity. An adorable little black boy ran by, and the girl looks at my daughter and says, “Ew. He looks creepy.” I paused and interjected, “That isn’t a very kind thing to say. Why does he look creepy to you?” I paused and interjected, “That isn’t a very kind thing to say. Why does he look creepy to you?” She replied, “Bc he’s like really black in the face”  *Awkward pause as I collect myself* She replied, “Bc he’s like really black in the face”  *Awkward pause as I collect myself* She continues… “Black is very bad. Light is much better. (As she points to her skin)” 1/4 She continues… “Black is very bad. Light is much better. (As she points to her skin)”",https://www.threads.com/@morganl.whit/post/DavpjikiTWO,"",0,0,0,0,NaN
